      "content": "okay, so the academic community says it \"contributes\" to innovation but can't even prove it helps the bottom line. if it's so hard to prove it actually helps the company, isn't it more accurate to say most of these massive corporate programs are just a way to avoid PR backlash rather than a real business strategy? it feels like the \"pro-DEI\" side is just hand-waving the lack of actual data.",
